{"user": "That thing where white kept passing after my a3 move - why did that happen exactly? Was I just filling the only squares white could use, or something else?", "user_ts": "2026-08-11T22:47:17.690521+00:00", "assistant": "White kept passing because **White had no legal move**.\n\nIn Othello, a player can only move if they can place a disc that **flips at least one opponent disc** \u2014 meaning it must trap a line of Black discs between the new White disc and an existing White disc.\n\nSo after your **a3** move, it wasn\u2019t just that you \u201cfilled White\u2019s squares\u201d; your move/flip pattern likely left White with **no empty square that could bracket and flip Black**. When that happens:\n\n- White **must pass** \u2014 passing is not optional.\n- Black keeps moving if Black still has legal moves.\n- White can pass multiple times in a row if Black\u2019s next moves still don\u2019t create any White legal move.\n\nCurrent board is full, so the game is over. Final count from the board: **Black 41, White 23** \u2014 Black wins by 18.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-11T22:47:17.690521+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-11T22:47:22.690521+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3, "Common Ground Question": 2}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0, "Common Ground Question": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "