{"user": "Was picking a1 before g2 the key reason white stayed stuck passing? Just want to understand that part for next time.", "user_ts": "2026-08-11T22:47:32.690521+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 **taking a1 before g2 was a key reason** White got stuck passing.\n\nWhy it mattered:\n\n- **a1 is permanent** once you take it; White can\u2019t flip it back.\n- It gave Black a stable anchor on the top/left, so White had fewer ways to \u201cbracket\u201d Black discs.\n- Then when you played moves like **g2/a3**, you weren\u2019t just flipping discs \u2014 you were leaving White with **no legal square that could flip anything**.\n- If you had played **g2 earlier**, it could have opened a corner/mobility chance for White instead.\n\nSo the lesson: **corner first, then mobility squeeze**. That\u2019s what made the pass chain happen.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-11T22:47:32.690521+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-11T22:47:37.690521+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 2, "Common Ground Question": 2, "Metacomment": 1}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.6666666666666666, "Common Ground Question": 0.6666666666666666, "Metacomment": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Common Ground Question", "Metacomment"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 1, "General Principle": 3, "Paraphrase": 1, "Positive Feedback": 2, "Neutral Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Local Justification": 1.0, "Wor